A||||4||Ferrari_cdn||How do I open the damn hood?||||11||
Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||09-12-2001||08:09 PM||||I know, I know, it's a stupid question.  I just got the car and it's in my garage now.  I haven't fiddled around the dashboard a lot yet but how the hell do I open the front hood and what is the LEFT/RIGHT vent handles for?||||reg||11
Z||000001||RedRavenGT||09-12-2001||08:21 PM||||Bottom left under the dash. Right underneath the vent is the lever for the hood.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>(formerly known as V8Fiero)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redraven.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ArchMagi||09-12-2001||08:21 PM||||Its right in front of the fuse box.  just pull it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>when sitting in the car, just take your left hand, smack it along the door, then foward and you should feel it np.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||09-12-2001||08:21 PM||||OK, to open the hood feel under the dash right below the left vent, this is the one to the left of the dash cluster. <P>If you get down and look you should see a handle that pulls down and back, that will pop the hood.<P>If for some reason the hood cable is broken you will also see a small wire with a kind of knob on the end clipped by the handle, this is the emergency pull for when the handle hookup breaks.<P>The left and right vent handles will operate the left or right vent which brings in outside air, I would guess you do not have A/C but just the heater for heat and the vents for cool air in the summer.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ferrari_cdn||09-12-2001||09:07 PM||||Oh now I found it easily.  Now I feel dumb.<P>Thanks guys.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
